#  HR Attrition Analytics & Prediction Dashboard

*LIFE DASHBOARD LINK:* https://datastudio.google.com/reporting/99ba624d-8f2a-4f35-9af2-326f3dc285b2/page/9g10F/edit

## Overview

This repository contains an end-to-end HR Attrition Analytics Dashboard designed to help business leaders 
and HR professionals identify key drivers behind employee turnover, evaluate compensation disparities, 
and analyze workforce tenure patterns.

The dashboard provides actionable insights into high-risk employee segments—such as those working overtime
or receiving lower monthly compensation—enabling proactive retention strategies.

##  Key Metrics & Insights
📌 Core Workforce KPIs
Total Employees: 1,470

Overall Attrition Rate: 16.12%

Average Monthly Income: €6,502.93

Average Tenure: 7.01 years

Main Analytical Views
1. Attrition by Department
Sales experiences the highest attrition rate at 20.63%, closely followed by Human Resources at 19.05%.

Research & Development demonstrates the highest retention stability with the lowest attrition rate at 13.84%.

2. Impact of Overtime on Attrition
Employees working overtime face a dramatically higher attrition rate (30.53%) compared to non-overtime staff (10.44%).

Overtime workload is identified as a primary trigger for employee departure.

3. Income Disparity vs. Turnover
Employees who stayed at the company have a significantly higher average monthly income (€6,832.74).

Employees who left earned an average monthly income of €4,787.09, highlighting compensation as a core retention factor.

4. Tenure vs. Attrition Breakdown
0–2 Years: Highest vulnerability window (102 departures out of 342 total employees in this cohort).

3–5 Years: 60 departures (out of 434 total).

6–10 Years: 55 departures (out of 448 total).

10+ Years: Highest stability (20 departures out of 246 total).

Features & Interactivity
Interactive Filters: Filter dataset views by Department, JobRole, Tenure Group, and OverTime status.

Multi-Tab Navigation:

HR Attrition Dashboard (Overview KPIs and key driver visuals)

Analytical Dashboard (Deep-dive breakdown)

Statistical Validation (Hypothesis testing and significance results)

Dashboard Preview
Technical Stack & Tools
Data Visualization / Dashboard: Looker Studio / Tableau / Power BI

Data Processing & Analysis: Python (Pandas, NumPy) / SQL

Statistical Analysis: Statistical significance testing (Hypothesis testing) on core HR metrics

#  Strategic Recommendations
Target Early Tenure (0–2 Years): Implement structured onboarding and 90-day review touchpoints to
reduce early-career churn.

Review Overtime Policies: Address burnout in departments with high overtime rates (particularly Sales) 
by reallocating workload or hiring supporting roles.

Re-evaluate Compensation Structures: Conduct competitive market rate adjustments for roles where 
departure rates correlate heavily with lower base pay.
